  "notes": "Interdisciplinary Baccalaureate (B.I.) in Psychology, effective Fall 2019, 120 credits, 10 terms. Transcribed verbatim from the official San Juan Campus Academic Catalog (August 2025 - July 2027) term-by-term sequence. CATALOG ANOMALIES (noted, not silently fixed): (1) The sequence table prints 'PSYU-419 Introduction to Neuropsychology' with prerequisite 'PSYU-407'; the program requirements table and the course description both confirm the real code is PSYU-439 (prereq PSYU-408). PSYU-407 does not exist in the course inventory, so the sequence-table code was NOT used; the plan records PSYU-439 with prereq PSYU-408. (2) SEMI-426 prereq conflict: the sequence table lists SEMI-424 while the course description lists PSYU-300/301/305/306; the plan records the union and notes it here. (3) The requirements table prints 'PSYU-300 Fundaments of Psychology' (typo); the sequence table and course description print 'Fundamentals of Psychology', which is used. (4) 'Interdisciplinary elective I' and 'Interdisciplinary elective II' are the two choice slots printed in the sequence tables as 'Interdisciplinary elective (1)' (Summer Year 1 and Fall Year 2); they are numbered here to keep codes unique since each lists a distinct option set. Course codes normalized to hyphenated uppercase form (catalog uses hyphens inconsistently); this is normalization, not invention. All per-semester credit sums and the 120-credit total verified against the catalog's printed totals.",
